WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.220
Mike Flanagan's adaptation of Stephen King's
novel features a strong cast of recognizable

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.780
actors, both major stars and supporting players
we've definitely seen before.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.920
Things are about to get eerie as we figure
out why the cast of Doctor Sleep looks so

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:13.460
familiar.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.760
The leader of the True Knot cult goes by "Rose
the Hat," and she looks to be a formidable

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.500
antagonist for Danny Torrance.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.699
In the film, Rose is played by Rebecca Ferguson,
who started acting in a Swedish soap opera,

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.320
but she's had plenty of stateside success
over the last decade.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.800
The Swedish actress is probably best known
for playing Ilsa Faust in the newer Mission:

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:32.920
Impossible films.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.841
She's also no stranger to horror roles, as
she appeared in Life as Miranda North and

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:38.420
The Snowman as Katrine Bratt.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.620
On top of all that, Ferguson has appeared
in movies ranging from The Greatest Showman

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.050
and The Kid Who Would Be King to Men in Black:
International and Florence Foster Jenkins.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.620
In other words, Ferguson is an in-demand actress,
talented, formidable, and the perfect pick

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.740
for such a terrifying Stephen King character.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.489
One of Danny's allies against the True Knot
is Billy Freeman, a man who helps our hero

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:01.480
cope with his alcoholism and fight against
his inner demons.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.860
He takes on a similar role to Dick Hallorann
from The Shining, serving as an older mentor

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.600
striving to help Danny with his trauma.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.700
In Doctor Sleep, veteran actor Cliff Curtis
portrays Billy Freeman.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.080
Curtis got his big break in 1999's Three Kings,
where he played Amir Abdulah.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.460
Since then, he's appeared in several movies
and shows, where he's played roles like Pablo

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.920
Escobar in Blow, Smiley in Training Day, and
Travis in Fear the Walking Dead.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.250
One of the most frightening members of the
True Knot is named Crow Daddy.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.320
He's Rose the Hat's lover and a sadistic,
terrifying individual.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.460
Doctor Sleep features an inspired bit of casting
for Crow Daddy, as he's played by Zahn McClarnon,

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.400
a man who lends plenty of gravitas to every
role he takes.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.020
McClarnon has been acting professionally for
more than 30 years, appearing in several television

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.080
shows in the '90s, as well as providing voicework
for several animated films.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.480
Over the years, he's started appearing in
larger roles, playing characters like Hanzee

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.000
in the Fargo television series and the Professor
in Bone Tomahawk.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.280
Probably his most recognizable role is that
of Akecheta, the leader of the Ghost Nation

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.180
tribe on HBO's Westworld.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.580
One of Danny's allies and close friends in
Doctor Sleep, Dr. John knows more about Danny

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:17.880
than pretty much anyone.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.000
He's aware that Danny possesses an extraordinary
ability, and he also knows that Danny isn't

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.330
the only one with the Shine.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.820
In the film, Dr. John is played by Bruce Greenwood,
and Greenwood is no stranger to playing roles

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.620
that require a commanding on-screen presence.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.440
Greenwood has played roles like John F. Kennedy
in Thirteen Days, the president of the United

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.460
States in Kingsman: The Golden Circle, and
Christopher Pike in the more recent Star Trek

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.000
films.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.780
He's also no stranger to Stephen King adaptations
directed by Mike Flanagan, since he played

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.980
Gerald in Gerald's Game.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:51.100
"And you did what you always do when it gets
too much, you ran in here."

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.940
Some of the True Knot have gained psychic
powers through their exposure to the Shine,

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.909
and Snakebite Andi is one of the most vicious
and formidable psychics imaginable.

00:02:59.909 --> 00:03:04.040
Andi has the power to make people fall into
a deep sleep with just a verbal suggestion.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.849
Snakebite Andi is played by Emily Alyn Lind
in Doctor Sleep, and acting is in her blood.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.010
Her mother is Barbara Alyn Woods, so Lind
got started acting at a very young age.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:17.050
She appeared as Shirley Temple in J. Edgar
and in several television series before the

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.620
age of ten.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:23.290
More recently, Lind appeared as Sophie Foster
in Replicas, Ariel on the CBS series Code

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.320
Black, and young Amanda Clarke on the ABC
series Revenge.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:31.140
Another member of the True Knot, Grampa Flick
kicks off the events of Doctor Sleep in a

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:31.960
lot of ways.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.300
Since the group strives to be immortal by
stealing the Shine from children, watching

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.200
a member of their cult grow older frightens
and infuriates the other members of the group.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:44.960
As to who portrays Grampa Flick, you've definitely
seen actor Carel Struycken in plenty of roles.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.170
Struycken has played monsters and odd characters
in many things, including the Giant in Twin

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.940
Peaks, Mr. Homn on Star Trek: The Next Generation,
the Moonlight Man in Gerald's Game, and the

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.480
bald Arquillian from Men in Black.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:00.360
One of his most memorable roles was as Lurch
in The Addams Family and Addams Family Values.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.129
But no matter the project, the seven-foot-tall
Dutchman always makes an impression when he

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:05.060
strides onto the screen.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.240
"It is happening again.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.640
It is happening again."

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:20.070
Without getting too heavy into spoiler territory,
the character of Lucy plays a small but important

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:20.980
role in Doctor Sleep.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:25.600
As such, the filmmakers needed to cast a confident
actress to take on the part, and they found

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.600
one in Jocelin Donahue.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.580
Donahue has made a pretty good name for herself
by taking on roles that seem thankless on

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.900
paper and making them memorable.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.280
Her horror credentials are certainly there.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.980
She played the young version of Lorraine in
Insidious: Chapter 2, and she won the Best

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.690
Actress award at LA Screamfest in 2009 for
the lead role in the indie darling The House

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.260
of the Devil.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.860
Silent Sarey is perhaps the most frightening
member of the True Knot due to her impressive

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:49.420
psychic gift.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.560
Sarey can essentially make people not realize
she's there.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.380
As long as they don't see her moving, she's
basically invisible.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.850
Silent Sarey is portrayed by Catherine Parker,
who certainly possesses the right combination

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.940
of charisma and threat to play the character.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.800
Early in her career, Parker found a good deal
of acclaim in the role of Callie in Absentia,

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.700
which led to memorable roles on shows like
Halt and Catch Fire and Masters of Sex.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:15.190
Recently, horror fans saw her as Poppy Hill,
the creepy flapper woman on Netflix's The

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.980
Haunting of Hill House, which was also directed
by Mike Flanagan.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.980
In Stephen King's novel, the character of
Deenie plays a big part in getting Danny to

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.440
the town where most of Doctor Sleep's action
takes place.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.320
It's a small but important role, but Chelsea
Talmadge [TALL-mij] is the perfect actress

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.120
to cast in such a pivotal role.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:34.780
The other projects that Talmadge is known
for generally gave her small scenes to play

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.810
with, and she managed to make them memorable.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.360
Talmadge appeared on the series Halt and Catch
Fire, playing Vera in six episodes of the

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:40.920
show.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.660
She also had a recurring role on the Billy
Ray Cyrus sitcom Still The King as Mabel.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.740
The role you're most likely to recognize her
from is Stranger Things.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:52.750
She played Carol, one of the students who
attend the pool party where Barb disappears,

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.520
and she later cheers on her boyfriend, Tommy,
and Steve Harrington when they break Jonathan

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.340
Byers' camera.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:05:59.640
"Dude!"

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.360
"Yeah, this isn't creepy at all."

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.120
Barry is a member of the True Knot, and he's
a reminder to the group of why it's so important

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.270
that they continue to feed off the Shine of
others.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:13.990
He's played in Doctor Sleep by Robert Longstreet,
who film fans have assuredly seen in something

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:14.600
over the years.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.960
Longstreet has been in around 80 roles in
his many years as an actor, but he's only

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.440
started to garner mainstream attention recently.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.990
He played Anderson in Boots Riley's bizarre
satire Sorry to Bother You, and he played

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.270
Professor James in Aquaman.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:30.480
He also has credits in Take Shelter, The Old
Man and the Gun, and Mohawk.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.630
Plus, horror hounds will recognize him as
Mr. Dudley, the kindly caretaker harboring

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.770
a dark secret in The Haunting of Hill House.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:40.610
If you're only familiar with the movie version
of The Shining, then you might be surprised

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.200
to see Dick Hallorann as a character in Doctor
Sleep.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.430
In the movie, Hallorann doesn't survive his
experience at the Overlook Hotel.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.820
However, he survives in the book, and Hallorann
still has a role to play in Danny's life when

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.000
the sequel rolls around.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.120
Carl Lumbly has been cast in the role that
Scatman Crothers played in the original Kubrick

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:56.560
film.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.840
Lumbly has had a huge variety of roles over
his career, including several voice acting

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.020
performances in cartoons and video games.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.250
As far as roles where he's actually shown
up on camera, Lumbly is probably best known

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.310
for playing Marcus Dixon on the show Alias.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:13.490
He played Mac Brashear in the film Men of
Honor, and he also features in a recurring

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.840
role on the Supergirl series.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:20.040
Another member of the True Knot, Apron Annie
has a very small role in Doctor Sleep.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.290
That said, you'll probably be snapping your
fingers and wracking your brain when you see

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.430
the actress who plays her, Selena Anduze,
up on the screen.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:29.880
You've definitely seen her in at least one
thing, and it's a place you've seen several

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.650
of the other actors in Doctor Sleep.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.860
Selena Anduze was in The Haunting of Hill
House.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:37.500
She only appeared in one episode, "The Twin
Thing," as a worker at the rehab facility.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.160
In fact, Anduze seems to almost exclusively
play doctors and detectives.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.460
You may also have seen Anduze in small roles
in movies like Venom, as the bistro manager,

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.900
or A Madea Family Funeral as the doctor.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:52.480
Anduze was supposed to have a fairly meaty
role in the DC series Swamp Thing as Caroline

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.720
Woodrue, but that show's swift cancellation
put a stop to that role.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.650
Doctor Sleep would hardly be the story of
Danny's coping with his childhood trauma if

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.060
his mother wasn't a part of things.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:06.820
In The Shining, Shelley Duvall played Wendy
Torrance with wide-eyed panic, and Alex Essoe

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.340
is taking on the role in Doctor Sleep.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.660
Essoe originally hails from Saudi Arabia,
and she's only been acting professionally

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.220
since 2008.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.180
She hasn't really had a big breakout role
at this point, but hopefully Doctor Sleep

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.500
will put her on the path to bigger and better
things.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.070
What Essoe does have is a lot of horror experience.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:26.300
She's appeared in indie horror films like
Starry Eyes, The Neighbour, Dark Intentions,

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.100
and Midnighters.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:31.120
She also appeared in The Drone, which is about
a drone that gains sentience and goes on a

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:31.660
killing spree.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.420
The True Knot in Doctor Sleep mostly preys
on children, so there are several roles that

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.400
Jacob Tremblay could be taking on.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.630
Considering Tremblay's impressive resume and
prior experience working with director Mike

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:46.340
Flanagan, it seems likely he's taking on a
substantial role in the film.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.640
Our money is on him playing young Danny Torrance.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:52.060
Regardless of what role Tremblay plays, we
know he's in the film, and you've probably

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.600
seen something else he's been in.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:57.580
He's actually done quite a bit of voice work,
but one of his biggest roles was alongside

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.160
Brie Larson in the critically acclaimed film
Room.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.630
Considering his impressive performance in
Room, it's hard to imagine Tremblay would

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.400
play just some random kid in Doctor Sleep.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.980
Tremblay has some other impressive credentials,
as well.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:12.380
He was Cody in Before I Wake, a prior collaboration
with Doctor Sleep director Mike Flanagan,

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.800
and he played Rory McKenna in The Predator.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:19.580
Chances are good that you don't need a reminder
about Ewan McGregor, the actor who plays the

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.330
grown-up Danny Torrance in Doctor Sleep.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.030
Of all the actors in the film, he's about
the only household name.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.760
If you somehow aren't able to put a film to
his face, though, here's what you've seen

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.300
him in.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.200
McGregor showed promise early on, stealing
the show in two impressive indie films: Shallow

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.900
Grave and Trainspotting.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:37.660
However, it was his casting as young Obi-Wan
Kenobi in the Star Wars prequels that shot

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.780
McGregor to superstardom.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:43.340
He also played Ed Bloom in Big Fish, Phillip
Morris in I Love You Phillip Morris, Christian

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:46.180
in Moulin Rouge, and the title character in
Christopher Robin.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.900
In other words, the dude is incredibly talented
and an impressive anchor for the cast of Doctor

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:50.440
Sleep.

